:name: STM32 NUCLEO-H753ZI - Virtual ECU Socket Co-Simulation Demo
:description: Boots a Zephyr CAN-networking sample on a Renode-simulated Nucleo H753ZI and exposes its UART over a TCP socket, so an external Python "hardware simulator" process can observe and interact with the virtual ECU the same way an external test harness talks to real hardware over a physical interface.

using sysbus

$bin=@https://dl.antmicro.com/projects/renode/nucleo_h743zi--zephyr-samples-net-sockets-can.elf-s_2243040-d8ba11b258437935c3880cf3e162f448f55c6f17

mach create "nucleo_h743zi"
include @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""

runMacro $reset

# Internal virtual CAN bus - a second simulated node could be attached here
# later to exchange UDS diagnostic frames with this ECU.
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"
connector Connect fdcan1 canHub

# Expose the ECU's UART over a TCP socket - this is the co-simulation seam.
# An external process (see hardware_simulator.py) connects here exactly like
# a real HIL test bench talks to a board over a physical UART/SPI link.
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 3456 "externalUART"
connector Connect sysbus.usart3 externalUART

start
